<title>UK: Argent says sells property for 22 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Argent says sells property for 22 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property development firm Argent Group Plc said on Thursday that it had sold one of its properties in Birmingham to the coal industry pension fund CIN for 22 million stg.</p>
<p>Argent said the property, Two Brindleyplace, totals 7,014 square metres and its sale reflects a net yield of around 6.7 percent. It is due for completion in June 1997.</p>
<p>Argent said the building has been pre-let to Lloyds Bank for 25 years with five yearly &quot;upward only&quot; rent reviews.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
